WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:05.540
<i>Train service has been suspended
for the rest of the day. I repeat...</i>

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.300
ADJUSTMENT WINDOW

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.810
<i>When I start walking, he starts walking.</i>

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:52.070
<i>When I stop, he stops.</i>

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.910
<i>It's like a god...</i>

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.450
<i>is quietly following me.</i>

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.010
White Storm (Part Four, Continued)

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:46.890
Um...

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.140
Well then...

00:03:58.570 --> 00:03:59.900
Thank you.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.650
I appreciate the help.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.030
Hello? Kiriyama here.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.780
<i>Hey! It's me.</i>

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.530
CHAIRMAN JINGUUJI

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.530
<i>Are you okay?</i>

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:47.780
Chairman?

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.080
Owww...

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.540
I was drinking until morning with the local
support group and sponsors, and just woke up.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.050
I heard the bullet train's shut down
because of the typhoon.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.420
So you okay? Where are you?

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:06.050
<i>In Sendai. It seems the train
won't be back in service today.</i>

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.430
I see.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:09.810
And, also...

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:12.180
On the same bullet train as you...

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.190
U-Umm...

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.310
You mean Mr. Souya?

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.320
He's fine. I'm with him right now.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:25.280
<i>Really! He's with you?</i>

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.070
<i>So you found a place to stay?</i>

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:32.830
Yes. It's the Seisen Inn near Sendai Station.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.870
Good to hear.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.710
So if you're with him, then...

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.210
Yeah.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:43.470
He can't hear.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.850
White Storm (Part Four, Continued)

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:59.860
White Storm (Part Five)

00:05:58.770 --> 00:05:59.860
Um...

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:02.110
When did it start?

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.740
Let's see. It's been a long time.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:10.490
Just over ten years.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:15.910
Throughout the years, there are times
when he can hear and times when he can't.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.800
He's been to doctors,
but they can't find the cause.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.630
"Stress" is the best they can come up with,
and can't figure anything else.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:33.810
And he being who he is,
went to the doctor regularly at first,

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:38.520
but then he started saying
he didn't mind the silence.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:40.770
But...

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.440
Even though he said that,
it can't be easy for him.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.490
I mean...

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.990
<i>I started to say, "When he talks to people..."</i>

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.240
<i>Then I remembered the train platform
in Morioka that morning.</i>

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.500
<i>I hadn't really seen him
do things with other people,</i>

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.340
<i>or seen him laugh or talk
with others either.</i>

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.380
<i>In my memories, he was always alone.</i>

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.220
<i>When was that?</i>

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:17.680
<i>It was a children's tournament, the first time
I won in the elementary school division.</i>

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.770
<i>If that's right...</i>

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.360
<i>If that's right, then by then...</i>

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.110
<i>he'd already...</i>

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.320
Um... Does anyone else...

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:34.530
<i>Yeah, well, the people
who play him a lot in matches.</i>

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:41.920
That being said, the only people who go up
against him are the challengers in title matches.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.670
That only leaves a handful of people.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:49.220
Well, he wasn't especially trying to hide it,

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:53.800
but there are some drawbacks to it,
so when I told him to keep quiet about it...

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.770
<i>I just have to finish the match
before the countdown, right?</i>

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.850
<i>Then, there shouldn't be any problems, right?</i>

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:02.310
That was his response.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:06.940
Geez, I'm worrying about the guy,
but he's carefree about it.

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:11.570
I mean, he's always been that kind of a person.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.950
So even when he says something
that's incoherent,

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.580
<i>I-I'm sorry!
Oh no! Your suit!</i>

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:19.580
people let it slide
because he was like that even before.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:26.250
As for the reception and Q&A before
and after matches, they tend to be similar

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.840
in terms of order and content.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.720
It's ironic that as he
became better and better at shogi,

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:35.760
people would look at him
like he was a little crazy,

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:42.690
but chalk it up to the eccentricity of a genius,
and even having fun with the mistaken notion.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:49.400
Well, if he's in his room now,
I'm sure he'll sleep through until morning.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.910
He'll be fine if you leave him alone.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.290
But to be honest, you were a big help.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:06.630
I was nervous about him walking around
in the rain, looking for a hotel.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:12.050
Right after this, he's got the Jeweled General
Tournament's best of seven matches.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:16.390
So you were a godsend
taking him with you like that.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:21.020
But listen, Kiriyama.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.390
I thought this back in Kyoto too.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.560
With Shimada...

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:28.860
<i>you were, how can I put it,
really good at looking after people.</i>

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.530
<i>Are you really a modern kid?</i>

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:33.240
<i>Have you been lying to us about being born
in the Heisei era, after 1989?</i>

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.660
<i>I bet you're really an obliging
middle-aged mother on the inside.</i>

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.070
I'm 18.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.660
Another thing. It was an entertaining match.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:49.460
You and Souya had a normal,
mutual understanding of each other.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.510
He kind of smiled.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:08.310
<i>When I woke up the next morning,
the typhoon had passed.</i>

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.820
Um, what do I owe you?

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:18.370
The man you came in with,
Mr. Souya, has paid for your stay.

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.160
<i>When I went outside,</i>

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:36.840
<i>Sendai's sky was a vast, fake-looking blue,
as if it were a giant canvas painted by a child.</i>

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:46.560
<i>It didn't feel real at all.</i>

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:53.940
<i>Yesterday's storm seemed far away,
as if it had happened in a dream.</i>

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:03.950
<i>Even though I'm certain
the two of us walked together in the rain.</i>

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:14.920
<i>I went to school from third period that day,</i>

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:17.800
<i>and maybe it was because I was tired,</i>

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.590
<i>but the teacher's voice
and usual classroom commotion</i>

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:26.600
<i>seemed vaguely distant,
so it didn't really get through to me.</i>

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:34.190
<i>And yet...</i>

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:41.410
<i>the sound of the pieces from that match...</i>

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:49.960
<i>I kept hearing it...</i>

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.540
<i>and it won't go away.</i>

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.340
SHOGI HALL

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:01.340
SHOGI HALL

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:07.100
Hey, Kiriyama.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:09.600
I heard how rough that typhoon was for you.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.270
Kiriyama?

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:18.190
What's with him? He's in a daze.

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:21.740
He's probably tired,
going straight from Sendai to school.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:26.030
You know, he probably had P.E.
That takes energy.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:27.910
OFFICE

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:38.170
APRIL JUNE

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:40.920
MAY

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.100
<i>I just couldn't...</i>

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:53.690
<i>get that sound...</i>

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.070
<i>out of my head.</i>

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.990
White Storm (Part Five)

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:05.990
Restart

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:08.990
Sis,

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:13.750
Kiriyama says he can't come over today either
because he has to prepare for a match tomorrow.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:13.250
Rei Kiriyama
Thank you for the invite

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:15.250
Oh, that's too bad.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:18.460
Even though this braised pork
came out really tender?

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.460
That's right!
Even though my specialty,

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:25.840
soft-boiled eggs, has been soaking
in the pork's salty-sweet sauce?

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:26.390
PLOOP

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:31.430
Yes! What's waiting for him are flavorful,
marinated soft-boiled eggs,

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:35.690
created with the ultimate soft-boiled eggs, from
the minds of the Kawamoto family's wisdom,

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:38.900
only discovered after dozens of failures!

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:40.280
MELTY

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:44.650
9 MIN   8 MIN   7 MIN   6 MIN

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:44.650
All so we could have a reliably slurried
soft-boiled egg to put on the table!

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.410
9 MIN

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.410
8MIN

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.410
7 MIN

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:45.410
6 MIN

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:49.160
9 MIN   8 MIN   7 MIN   6 MIN

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:49.160
Does he have any idea how much time
went into perfecting that?

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:55.000
I've got it, Sis. It's eight minutes!

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.130
Got it. Eight minutes, huh?

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:01.250
Medium-sized eggs, taken right out of the fridge,
in boiling water for eight minutes!

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:05.010
FFFGGGRR

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:05.010
Caught up
in the
excitement

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:05.010
MWAAARR

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:12.390
The Kawamoto Family's Manual
for Absolutely Successful Soft-Boiled Eggs!

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:16.560
Step one.
Take your eggs right out of the refrigerator.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:20.900
Since we're often in a hurry, it's faster
to take them out of the fridge and into the pot.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:24.650
Step two.
Make a small hole in the bottom of the egg.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:26.280
The flat part is the bottom.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.280
TA-DAA

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.030
A tool for poking holes in eggs!

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:32.450
Poking a hole in it reduces the chances
of the egg cracking in the pot.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:34.040
You can also use a thumbtack!

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.960
ROLL ROLL

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:37.330
Step Three.
Boil the eggs in boiling water for eight minutes.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:41.000
For about the first two minutes,
lightly roll them around with chopsticks!

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.670
The yolk will come to the center!

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.420
Ssssss

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.220
Step four.
Cool them off in cold water.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:49.050
If you don't, the inside will continue to cook!

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:50.800
Mmmm!

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:54.560
IN STEW

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:54.560
IN CURRY

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.560
The result is a life
with always reliable soft-boiled eggs!

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.440
AS IS, ON TOP OF RICE

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.440
IN POTATO SALAD

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.440
It took so long to perfect.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.940
We couldn't get the hardness
to be consistent because

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.690
we had "eggs that returned to room temperature"
and "eggs right from the refrigerator."

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:07.070
Having both mixed up the level of hardness!

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:08.320
But now...

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:11.570
BAAAM

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.570
we have the power of a new pressure cooker,

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:14.160
which we won in
a neighborhood association drawing recently!

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:18.460
SAMPLING

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:21.460
How could I have wasted all that time, effort,
and high gas bills on endless stove-cooking?

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:25.420
I had no idea that we could be eating
juicy braised pork in just 20 minutes!

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:27.090
WEEPING

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:27.090
SPELLBOUND

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:35.270
And this pork belly, only 58 yen per 100 grams.
I was able to buy one kilogram for 580 yen!

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:31.720
PIPING HOT

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:38.350
For 580 yen, we can eat as much as we like!

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.980
RICH

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:40.980
TENDER SHINY

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.980
Thank you for the food!

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:47.110
Pork belly over rice is the best!

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.990
D-Delicious!

00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:01.120
How could Mr. Glasses miss out
on something so good?

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.420
It's a crying shame!

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:08.880
But we can make it again.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.220
And maybe next time it'll be even better.

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.010
Yummy!

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:16.010
I just remembered!

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.020
I got a photo from Chiho!

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.980
These puppies are just adorable!

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:23.980
Oh, let me see!

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.650
They're Hana's babies!

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:30.150
You can tell how fluffy they are!

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.370
There are five pups!
I can't wait to see them in person!

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:01.520
Kiriyama.

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:03.900
Kiriyama.

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:05.810
Kiriyama!

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.070
Hey, Kiriyama!

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:13.360
You little...

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:16.530
Kiriyama, you bastard!

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:22.250
Oh, g-good morning, Mr. Shimada.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:22.250
GRIT
GRIT
GRIT

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:24.000
After-effect of the shock

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:28.290
What are you, an elementary school student
playing a video game while walking?

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.760
I'm confiscating this!
I mean, game records?

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:36.640
TOUJI SOUYA

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:41.890
You had fun, huh?

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:46.520
Your match with Souya.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:52.110
You want to see him again, right?

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:55.320
In front of the board.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.120
I know how it is.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.290
SHOGI HALL

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:04.290
Oh yeah.

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.790
Nikaidou is out of the hospital.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:11.840
Nikaidou.

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:16.680
Yeah. He'll make it to the first qualifying round
for the Jeweled King Tournament in two days.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:20.560
Huh? Nikaidou is okay already?

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:25.060
SHOGI HALL

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:25.060
Playing right after being discharged
from the hospital? Will he be okay?

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:31.070
Why don't you drop in on him?

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:36.030
Even though this is his first year being promoted
to C-1 from the rank-deciding competitions,

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:38.870
he already has two black marks
for default losses due to absence.

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:42.580
He was really enthusiastic about it before,
so I imagine he's depressed now.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:48.920
<i>You play ten rank-deciding matches per year.</i>

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:52.170
<i>There are 34 people in our C-1 class.</i>

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:56.260
<i>Every year, the top two are promoted.</i>

00:18:56.680 --> 00:19:00.600
<i>In one out of every five, the one with
the lowest results gets a demotion point.</i>

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:04.560
<i>If the player gets two demotion points,
they're demoted.</i>

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:07.060
<i>I won the final match!</i>

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:09.980
<i>So I'll be Class C-1 next term,
the same level as you!</i>

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:12.230
<i>Don't lose along the way!</i>

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:15.610
<i>Because you and I
are going to create a legend!</i>

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:21.490
I'm sure he hasn't fully recovered yet,

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:27.040
but just seeing you again
would probably cheer him up a bit.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.080
<i>Nikaidou.</i>

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.000
<i>He must be so discouraged.</i>

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.010
<i>He was in such high spirits before.</i>

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:41.260
<i>Take better care of your shogi, and yourself!</i>

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:47.520
<i>I made a comeback because of
those words that he said to me then.</i>

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:59.070
Huh? What are you doing here, Kiriyama?

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:01.740
You don't have a match today, do you?

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:05.410
No. I, um... You know.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:09.910
SHOGI HALL

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:28.180
UNKAKU ROOM

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:27.430
<i>This is taking a while.</i>

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:34.310
<i>Is he doing okay?</i>

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.320
<i>Nikaidou.</i>

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:49.330
I lost.

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.340
Damn it!

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.800
You little brat!

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:04.090
I never should've worried about you!
Ugh, geez!

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:06.510
That was awesome, Nikaidou!

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:09.890
Right out of the hospital
and he beats Aono 8th-Dan!

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:15.440
He played the King to 7-9
with a One-Turn Loss Bishop Exchange!

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:17.110
That's a new method!

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:19.570
I see.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:22.570
If you place the King to 7-9 here,

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:25.070
then my Rook can't keep going.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:29.620
Were you thinking about this
when you were in the hospital?

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:31.830
Damn it!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:34.830
I see! The King to 7-9, huh?

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:37.590
PAT
PAT

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:42.720
It'll be okay
Nikaidou!

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:38.590
I carried you that day and laid you down,

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:42.720
SUPER
NICE GUY

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:42.720
The ambulance will
 be here any minute!

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:42.720
then ran all over the place looking
for Mr. Hanaoka. I was so worried about you!

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.720
Hold on!

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:42.720
I'll go find
your butler!

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:46.180
- But now this?
- Y-Yes, sir!

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:48.930
Thank you for taking care of me that day!

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:51.980
So, that move!

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:54.690
Do you think they'll name that move after me?

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:59.360
Not if I have any say in it!
I'll study it and come up with countermeasures!

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:03.110
YELL
YELL
YELL

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:03.110
DAZED

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:04.610
Kiriyama!

00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:07.370
DAZED

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:07.370
Did you see my awesome move?

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:10.450
I've been thinking about that
for the longest time!

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:12.830
And I finally got the chance to try it out today!

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:15.620
Instead of the usual like
Gold to 7-8 or Pawn to 2-4,

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:19.210
the attack will go smoother with King to 7-9!

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:22.760
What do you think? Will they name it after me?

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:25.220
Maybe the "Nikaidou Vaccine"?

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:30.140
It's been my aspiration to create
a technique that'll leave my name on it!

00:22:30.930 --> 00:22:33.430
<i>I imagine he's depressed now.</i>

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:40.610
What?!

00:22:40.610 --> 00:22:42.070
What are you laughing at?

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:54.450
What? What's so funny, Kiriyama?!

00:22:56.040 --> 00:23:00.040
Restart

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.430
Episode 39

00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:34.640
But it really helped that you came.

00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:37.430
Of course I'll do my best
with the commentary!

00:24:37.430 --> 00:24:39.980
I'm delighted to see you all
again this year.

00:24:39.980 --> 00:24:42.190
Thank you, everyone!

00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:43.940
Wh-What is this?

00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:47.860
I want it, even if I have to
sink my teeth into it.

00:24:48.190 --> 00:24:50.030
My first title, that is.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:59.040
ILLUSTRATION:
MIKI TORI

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:54.240
Harunobu Nikaidou is totally back!

00:24:54.240 --> 00:24:57.990
Eat this! It's the Nikaidou Vaccine!
